# Cursor Rules for E-commerce Project

## Code Quality & Error Handling

### Shell Scripts & Pre-commit Hooks
- Always use error checking for directory changes: `cd directory || exit 1` instead of just `cd directory`
- This prevents silent failures when directories don't exist or cd fails
- Apply this pattern to all shell scripts, especially in pre-commit hooks

### TypeScript/JavaScript
- Remove unused imports and variables
- Add proper error handling for async operations
- Use proper type definitions for all props and state

### React Best Practices
- Always include all dependencies in useEffect dependency arrays or disable the rule with a comment
- Remove unused variables and imports
- Ensure all imported components are actually used

## Project Structure
- Follow the existing folder structure: `client/src/` for frontend, `server/` for backend
- Keep API endpoints organized by feature in `services/endPoints/`
- Use TypeScript interfaces for all data structures

## Git & Commits
- Run pre-commit hooks before committing (linting, type checking)
- Fix all linting errors before committing
- Use meaningful commit messages

